                <head>Appendix 197</head>
                <p rendition="#center">[<hi rendition="#italic">Telegram From the American Belief
                        Administration at Hamburg Regarding Shipments of</hi>] <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cotton for Poland</hi></p>
                <p>The following telegram from Colonel Coombs, American Belief Administration
                    Representative at Hamburg, was received on the 12th June:— <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“German Government not willing to allow shipment of cotton to Poland
                            through Danzig unless they get portion. Their idea is 10 per cent., to
                            cover transportation charges and as payment for privilege of passage
                            through this country. Coombs.”</p></quote></p>
            </div>
